. Adoran a","height":0.017496907451669652},{"height":0.017473482874302393,"text":"Ram (el rey ideal y el hombre","width":0.3051546456473214,"y":0.5828488376806333,"x":0.5587628803103599},{"text":"perfecto, representando justicia,","x":0.558762895959131,"y":0.5639534888942281,"width":0.34639174107142856,"height":0.019044093793673778},{"y":0.5430075427631168,"width":0.36954914202008926,"x":0.5585217072006267,"height":0.02179949865717734,"text":"virtud y dharma), y Vishnu (uno de"},{"x":0.5567010441172104,"y":0.5261627911980751,"text":"los dioses principales del hinduismo).","width":0.40206183733258927,"height":0.01744185946431498},{"text":"También adoran otros dioses como","x":0.5587628845291216,"y":0.5087209302117153,"width":0.36907216099330353,"height":0.014647320909523143},{"x":0.5587628869848046,"height":0.016116035455277955,"text":"Kali, Durga y Hanuman. Celebran","y":0.48831587465930015,"width":0.3484536132812499},{"x":0.5587628874983316,"width":0.3525773228236607,"height":0.017472311722281253,"text":"grandes festivales hindúes, como","y":0.4680232563974106},{"height":0.018946882028141654,"text":"Diwali, Holi, Shivaratri y Dussehra.","x":0.5587628912880269,"width":0.3608247419084821,"y":0.44762288514594417},{"text":"Hay muy poco cristianismo entre los","y":0.4102018877913429,"height":0.021143812599151435,"x":0.5585153178268663,"width":0.3819078543526786},{"text":"kurmi. La mayoría de los kurmi sigue","y":0.39242546351829977,"width":0.38144328962053575,"height":0.0174582571295554,"x":0.5587628906794228},{"x":0.558762891732327,"width":0.34639174107142856,"text":"el hinduismo. Unos pocos se han","height":0.016116035455278066,"y":0.37348912189148453},{"height":0.017471140570260224,"text":"convertido al cristianismo, pero no es","y":0.35319767474458663,"x":0.5587628955977655,"width":0.39381441824776786},{"x":0.5587628832602632,"text":"común. La comunidad kurmi tiene","y":0.33561643851604817,"width":0.3567010323660714,"height":0.01612774774396153},{"x":0.5567010372571